  "worked_solution": "First, let's add a new column to our table and compute the ratio of cars per hour for each row.     \n\n| Hours ($t$) | Cars ($n$) | Cars / Hours |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $4$ | $4$ |\n| $3$ | $12$ | $4$ |\n| $5$ | $20$ | $4$ |\n\nThe ratio of cars per hour is the same for each row. Therefore, there is a proportional relationship between $n$ and $t.$ The constant of proportionality is $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III  only.\"",
